      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X\\sim U[2,8],$ find $\\textrm{E}[X].$",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=2$ and $b=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\dfrac{2+8}{2} =5.\n$$",
